Michelle's Entry:
In this lab for all the types of ML I think Reinforcement Learning caught my attention the most because the system learns along with the user
and the feedback it gets keeps improving it over time, instead of just learning from data 
it was given upfront (supervised and unsupervised learning).
The most challenging part was figuring out which type of learning fits which issue.
If I were to apply these concept for my field of interest I would say music I'm interested in music 
Supervised Learning already powers music recommendation on platforms like Spotify or Apple Music, predicting songs 
I'd like from labeled listening history, like Spotify or Apple Music. Unsupervised Learning could group songs by 
sound or style without predefined genres. Reinforcement Learning could work for an AI composing music, 
learning over time which melodies get better feedback.
